# ── CROSS-ORIGIN ISOLATION ── these two headers are what make SharedArrayBuffer available, which is the
# prerequisite for the generation workers writing terrain straight into the world grid instead of handing
# slabs back for the main thread to memcpy (measured: 1,900 ms per 20 s of sprinting, all on one thread).
#
# VERIFY, don't assume: load the game, open the console and type   crossOriginIsolated
#   true   → it worked; SharedArrayBuffer is now available
#   false  → Apache ignored this file (nginx, or mod_headers off) — set it at Cloudflare instead
#
# IF THE SITE BREAKS (missing images, fonts, embeds from other domains), require-corp is the cause: it
# blocks every cross-origin subresource that has not opted in. Swap it for `credentialless`, which gives
# the same isolation without that requirement. The game itself is self-contained — no external scripts or
# stylesheets, and every runtime fetch is same-origin under assets/ — so it is anything ELSE on the site
# that would object.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header always set Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy "same-origin"
  Header always set Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy "require-corp"
</IfModule>
